{"content":[{"c":["FULLER’S FIELD*"],"sourceClass":"h1","t":"p"},{"c":["Place outside Jerusalem that was linked to a spring or pool by a causeway or aqueduct (",{"href":"?bref=2Kgs.18.17","r":"2Kgs.18.17","rawR":"2Kgs.18.17","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"2Kgs.18.17","value":"2Kgs.18.17"}],"t":"ref","v":"2 Kgs 18:17"},"; ",{"href":"?bref=Isa.7.3","r":"Isa.7.3","rawR":"Isa.7.3","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"Isa.7.3","value":"Isa.7.3"}],"t":"ref","v":"Is 7:3"},"; ",{"href":"?bref=Isa.36.2","r":"Isa.36.2","rawR":"Isa.36.2","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"Isa.36.2","value":"Isa.36.2"}],"t":"ref","v":"36:2"},"). It has been generally identified with an area near En-rogel (“spring of the fuller”). The spring was south of Jerusalem in the Kidron Valley. It was originally the tribal boundary between Judah and Benjamin (",{"href":"?bref=Josh.15.7","r":"Josh.15.7","rawR":"Josh.15.7","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"Josh.15.7","value":"Josh.15.7"}],"t":"ref","v":"Jos 15:7"},"; ",{"href":"?bref=Josh.18.16","r":"Josh.18.16","rawR":"Josh.18.16","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"Josh.18.16","value":"Josh.18.16"}],"t":"ref","v":"18:16"},"). When Absalom rebelled and King David fled from Jerusalem, two of David’s men stayed at En-rogel to gather information about the rebellion (",{"href":"?bref=2Sam.17.17","r":"2Sam.17.17","rawR":"2Sam.17.17","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"2Sam.17.17","value":"2Sam.17.17"}],"t":"ref","v":"2 Sm 17:17"},")."],"sourceClass":"fl","t":"p"},{"c":["En-rogel has been identified with the modern Bir Attub, or “Job’s Well,” on the left bank of Wadi en-Nar. The well sinks deep into the rock, reaches an underground stream, and gushes forth following rainfalls."],"sourceClass":"","t":"p"},{"c":[{"c":["See also"],"sourceClass":"ital","t":"span"}," ",{"href":"?item=Jerusalem_Article_TyndaleOpenBibleDictionary","id":"Jerusalem_Article_TyndaleOpenBibleDictionary","rawId":"Jerusalem_Article_TyndaleOpenBibleDictionary","t":"link","v":"Jerusalem"},"."],"sourceClass":"","t":"p"}],"format":"bsb-study-dictionary-v2","id":"FullersField","provenance":{"archiveSha256":"10758ea00dbea7540f9337e43e59c8e4000295c1261e3426bab6f31c31dcff5b","release":"1.6","sourceCitationReferences":[{"anchorText":"2 Kgs 18:17","canonicalization":"deferred_to_dictionary_mapping_workstream","hrefExact":"?bref=2Kgs.18.17","rawQueryValue":"2Kgs.18.17","sourceRefExact":"2Kgs.18.17"},{"anchorText":"Is 7:3","canonicalization":"deferred_to_dictionary_mapping_workstream","hrefExact":"?bref=Isa.7.3","rawQueryValue":"Isa.7.3","sourceRefExact":"Isa.7.3"},{"anchorText":"36:2","canonicalization":"deferred_to_dictionary_mapping_workstream","hrefExact":"?bref=Isa.36.2","rawQueryValue":"Isa.36.2","sourceRefExact":"Isa.36.2"},{"anchorText":"Jos 15:7","canonicalization":"deferred_to_dictionary_mapping_workstream","hrefExact":"?bref=Josh.15.7","rawQueryValue":"Josh.15.7","sourceRefExact":"Josh.15.7"},{"anchorText":"18:16","canonicalization":"deferred_to_dictionary_mapping_workstream","hrefExact":"?bref=Josh.18.16","rawQueryValue":"Josh.18.16","sourceRefExact":"Josh.18.16"},{"anchorText":"2 Sm 17:17","canonicalization":"deferred_to_dictionary_mapping_workstream","hrefExact":"?bref=2Sam.17.17","rawQueryValue":"2Sam.17.17","sourceRefExact":"2Sam.17.17"}],"sourceItemFragmentSha256":"d7ee13b8d92fe849d95e079d8fa926e5319d234f7ddfa13da473995f97562ab9","sourceItemName":"FullersField","sourceItemOrder":91,"sourceMember":"Articles/F.xml","supplementPointersNotIncludedAsContent":[]},"sourceAttributes":{"name":"FullersField","product":"TyndaleOpenBibleDictionary","typename":"Article"},"sourceTitleExact":"Fuller’s Field*","title":"Fuller’s Field*","version":"v2-a101d843a2f0cd3fc0c6"}